# BUGS

`<pthread.h>` has no `pthread_cancel`, `pthread_kill`, `pthread_sigmask`, `pthread_atfork`, barriers, spin locks, `pthread_setname_np`, scheduling or affinity calls, `pthread_attr_setguardsize`, `pthread_attr_setstack`, `PTHREAD_STACK_MIN`, rwlock attribute functions, robust or process-shared mutexes, or priority protocols.
`pthread_rwlock_timedrdlock` and `timedwrlock` are not there either.
The stack size of an attribute object has no effect.
A deadlock on a normal mutex or on a read-write lock is not detected.
